# Normalise line endings before Git ever sees them.
#
# Why: on Windows, editors and AI tools happily write CRLF. A mixed-line-ending repo shows
# up as whole-file diffs on CI, wrecks review diffs, and makes `ruff format --check` fail
# for reasons that have nothing to do with the actual change. 33 files were CRLF on the
# first real lint run (C22).
#
# Rule: everything is LF in the repository, regardless of platform.

* text=auto eol=lf

# Binary - never touch
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.jpeg binary
*.gif binary
*.pdf binary
*.mp4 binary
*.mov binary
*.webm binary
*.onnx binary
*.pdmodel binary
*.pdparams binary
*.db binary

# Kept as-is
*.bat text eol=crlf
*.ps1 text eol=crlf
